17. PROVIDER ABSTRACTION
==================================================

Create:

    interface LlmProvider {
      generateStructured<T>(
        request: StructuredGenerationRequest<T>
      ): Promise<StructuredGenerationResult<T>>;
    }

The request should include:

- stage
- system prompt
- user content
- response schema
- model
- max output tokens
- temperature or equivalent
- abort signal

The result should include:

- validated output
- raw response metadata
- input token usage if available
- output token usage if available
- duration
- provider
- model

Use structured output where supported.

Otherwise extract JSON carefully and validate it.

On schema failure:

1. Record the failure.
2. Attempt one bounded repair request.
3. If still invalid, fail that stage as inconclusive.
4. Never silently coerce dangerous malformed output.

==================================================
18. CONTEXT SELECTION AND TOKEN CONTROL
==================================================

Do not send the entire repository blindly.

Build a context selector.

Always consider:

- diff
- changed files
- package manifests
- nearby code around changed lines
- imported/local dependencies when reasonably resolvable
- tests associated with changed modules
- README/project configuration

Exclude:

- node_modules
- vendor
- dist/build
- generated files
- binary files
- lockfiles from full LLM context unless dependency changes matter
- secrets
- oversized files unless a relevant slice can be selected

Track estimated and actual token use.

Implement hard context limits.

If context is truncated, stages must report that limitation.

==================================================
19. PRIVACY AND SAFETY
==================================================

Verik handles private source code.

Requirements:

- Never include environment variable values in prompts.
- Redact likely secrets from diffs and logs.
- Exclude configured sensitive paths.
- Print a clear local warning before the first remote-model run.
- Add configuration for provider disablement/offline mode.
- Never execute code suggested by an LLM.
- Builder commands come only from deterministic detection/configuration.
- Never let Scout/Reviewer dynamically invent shell commands that are executed without deterministic approval.
- Prevent path traversal in local report storage.
- Bound logs, diffs, outputs, and timeouts.
- Do not follow symlinks outside the repository when collecting context.
- Never mutate source files during verification stages.

==================================================
20. ERROR HANDLING
==================================================

Handle:

- not inside Git repository
- unborn repository/no commits
- detached HEAD
- dirty working tree
- no changes produced
- wrapped command missing
