==================================================

- Do not leave placeholder implementations disguised as complete.
- Do not use `any` unless an external boundary makes it unavoidable and it is narrowed immediately.
- Validate every external boundary.
- Prefer small explicit modules.
- Avoid giant manager classes.
- Use dependency injection where it improves testing, not everywhere.
- Keep domain logic independent from CLI presentation.
- No network calls in unit tests.
- Never execute LLM-produced shell commands.
- Never upload secrets.
- Never claim a stage passed when it did not execute.
- Never hide limitations.
- Every verdict must trace back to evidence.
- Every finding must cite evidence.
- The Judge must be able to dismiss Reviewer findings.
- Keep the initial implementation understandable by one founder.

